.TH DHCP-LEASE-LIST 8 "2026-06-02" "dhcp-oru-toolkit 2.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
dhcp-lease-list \- display ISC or Kea DHCP IPv4 and IPv6 leases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dhcp-lease-list
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dhcp-lease-list
reads ISC DHCP (\fIdhcpd.leases\fR / \fIdhcpd6.leases\fR) or Kea DHCP
(\fIkea-leases4.csv\fR / \fIkea-leases6.csv\fR) lease databases and prints a
unified, color-coded view of IPv4 and IPv6 leases. It extracts the client MAC
address from DHCPv6 DUIDs (DUID-LLT, DUID-EN, DUID-LL) where possible and
de-duplicates Kea journal CSVs so that the last active entry per IP wins.
.PP
With
.B \-\-conflicts
it additionally reports lease conflicts: a single MAC holding multiple active
IP addresses, or a single IP address held by multiple active MACs \(em the
signature of the O-RU shared-xid IP-theft defect.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-server {isc,kea}
DHCP server type (default: isc). Selects the default lease file paths.
.TP
.B \-\-v4\-lease \fIFILE\fR
Path to the IPv4 lease file (overrides the default for the selected server).
.TP
.B \-\-v6\-lease \fIFILE\fR
Path to the IPv6 lease file (overrides the default for the selected server).
.TP
.B \-\-v4\-only
Show IPv4 leases only.
.TP
.B \-\-v6\-only
Show IPv6 leases only.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Show all leases, including expired and free.
.TP
.B \-\-state {active,free,expired,declined,released}
Filter leases by binding state.
.TP
.B \-\-conflicts
After listing, scan the parsed leases for conflicts (one MAC holding multiple
active IPs, or one IP held by multiple active MACs) and print them. Exits
non-zero (2) if any HIGH-severity conflict is found.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the program version and exit.
.SH DEFAULT LEASE FILES
.TP
.B ISC
/var/lib/dhcp/dhcpd.leases and /var/lib/dhcp/dhcpd6.leases
.TP
.B Kea
/var/lib/kea/kea-leases4.csv and /var/lib/kea/kea-leases6.csv
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
List active ISC leases (IPv4 and IPv6):
.B dhcp-lease-list
.TP
Show every lease including expired/free:
.B dhcp-lease-list \-\-all
.TP
Read Kea CSV databases:
.B dhcp-lease-list \-\-server kea
.TP
Inspect specific lease files and only IPv4:
.B dhcp-lease-list \-\-v4\-only \-\-v4\-lease /tmp/dhcpd.leases
.TP
Flag IP-theft-style conflicts:
.B dhcp-lease-list \-\-conflicts
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success and non-zero on error (for example, an unreadable lease
file).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dhcp-forensics (8),
.BR dhcpd (8),
.BR kea-dhcp4 (8)
.SH AUTHOR
labuser, as part of dhcp-oru-toolkit.
